IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `whsnt-dates`

-- Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) -- the provisions a person bringing or answering a
-- claim meets, asked from the seat of the individual.
--
-- SEAT: the individual the law is applied to: the worker hurt, or put at risk, at work, and their family; the worker,
-- prospective worker or other person punished, pressured or misled for a safety reason (Part 6); the person who wants a
-- prosecution brought (ss 231 to 232, 34E); the worker affected by an inspector's or the regulator's decision (Part 12);
-- the person whose loss an inspector's powers caused (s 184); the worker with a contract term or a charge about safety
-- (ss 267, 272, 273). The regulator (the Work Health Authority, s 4), inspectors, the Director of Public Prosecutions
-- and the Work Health Court get no seat: what they must do appears as what the person is owed, and by when.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list). No question takes a DEONTIC or an
-- EVENT. The two duties with a period the person meets (the regulator's notice under s 231(5), the business's
-- prohibition under s 273) are regulative rules run by EVALTRACE inside a question.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: ss 35 to 37 (notifiable incident, serious injury or illness, dangerous incident); ss 84, 88, 103
-- (ceasing unsafe work); Part 6 whole (ss 104 to 115, with the penalties of ss 104, 107, 108 and 109); the maximum
-- penalties of ss 31, 32, 33 and 34B; ss 231, 231A(1), 231B, 232 and 34E (asking for a prosecution, the DPP's part, the
-- limitation period); s 184; Part 12 (ss 223, 224, 226, 228(1) to (5), 229(1) to (3), 229B(1), (2)); s 267; s 272;
-- s 273. What is out, and why, is in NOTES.md.
--
-- Edition: Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT), Act No. 39 of 2011, reprint REPW025 as
-- in force at 1 February 2020 (the current reprint on 6 November 2026), deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/Work-Health-and-Safety-National-Uniform-Legislation-Act-2011-NT-current-reprint-REPW025.txt.
-- The NT Act states its penalties in dollars in each section (no schedule, no indexation), except industrial
-- manslaughter by a body corporate (65 000 penalty units), whose value in dollars is set by the Penalty Units Act and is
-- not computed here. The Regulations (not deposited) can add or exclude kinds of serious injury and dangerous incident
-- (ss 36, 37) and make decisions reviewable (s 223 item 13): those answers are NOTHING.
--
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from an unofficial copy under
-- the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Judgments the Act hands to someone else are INPUTS. Answers follow
-- the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (NOTES.md): JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words,
-- NOTHING where it does not answer.

§ `Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT): a claimant's questions`

§§ `Part 3 -- was it a notifiable incident` -- arises only if someone died, was hurt or was put in danger at work

-- s 36: "serious injury or illness of a person means an injury or illness requiring the person to have: (a) immediate
-- treatment as an in-patient in a hospital; or (b) immediate treatment for: (i) the amputation of any part of his or her
-- body; or (ii) a serious head injury; or (iii) a serious eye injury; or (iv) a serious burn; or (v) the separation of
-- his or her skin from an underlying tissue (such as degloving or scalping); or (vi) a spinal injury; or (vii) the loss
-- of a bodily function; or (viii) serious lacerations; or (c) medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a
-- substance; and includes any other injury or illness prescribed by the Regulations, but does not include an illness or
-- injury of a prescribed kind."
DECLARE `What the injury or illness needed` IS ONE OF
    `immediate treatment as an in-patient in a hospital (s 36(a))`
    `immediate treatment for an amputation of any part of the body (s 36(b)(i))`
    `immediate treatment for a serious head injury (s 36(b)(ii))`
    `immediate treatment for a serious eye injury (s 36(b)(iii))`
    `immediate treatment for a serious burn (s 36(b)(iv))`
    `immediate treatment for skin separated from the tissue under it, such as degloving or scalping (s 36(b)(v))`
    `immediate treatment for a spinal injury (s 36(b)(vi))`
    `immediate treatment for the loss of a bodily function (s 36(b)(vii))`
    `immediate treatment for serious lacerations (s 36(b)(viii))`
    `medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance (s 36(c))`
    `none of these`
    `there was no injury or illness`

-- s 37: "dangerous incident means an incident in relation to a workplace that exposes a worker or any other person to a
-- serious risk to the person's health or safety emanating from an immediate or imminent exposure to: (a) ... (l) any
-- other event prescribed by the Regulations; but does not include an incident of a prescribed kind."
DECLARE `What the incident exposed people to` IS ONE OF
    `an uncontrolled escape, spillage or leakage of a substance (s 37(a))`
    `an uncontrolled implosion, explosion or fire (s 37(b))`
    `an uncontrolled escape of gas or steam (s 37(c))`
    `an uncontrolled escape of a pressurised substance (s 37(d))`
    `electric shock (s 37(e))`
    `the fall or release from a height of any plant, substance or thing (s 37(f))`
    `the collapse, overturning, failure or malfunction of, or damage to, plant that must be authorised for use (s 37(g))`
    `the collapse or partial collapse of a structure (s 37(h))`
    `the collapse or failure of an excavation or its shoring (s 37(i))`
    `an inrush of water, mud or gas in workings, an underground excavation or a tunnel (s 37(j))`
    `the interruption of the main ventilation in an underground excavation or tunnel (s 37(k))`
    `something else`
    `there was no such exposure`

-- s 35: "notifiable incident means: (a) the death of a person; or (b) a serious injury or illness of a person; or (c) a
-- dangerous incident." A "means" definition; but ss 36 and 37 each add kinds the Regulations prescribe, and exclude kinds
-- the Regulations prescribe, and the Regulations are not deposited. So: a listed head and not an excluded kind is JUST
-- TRUE; an excluded kind is JUST FALSE ("does not include"); outside the listed heads the Regulations may still add it,
-- and the answer is NOTHING (it points outside the sources).
@export Was what happened at work a "notifiable incident" -- a death, a serious injury or illness, or a dangerous incident -- that the business must report to the regulator immediately (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 35 to 38)? Yes, no, or (NOTHING) not answered without the Regulations.
GIVEN `a person died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person die?
      `what the injury or illness needed` IS A `What the injury or illness needed` @desc If someone was injured or became ill, what treatment did it require? Choose the first that fits.
      `what the incident exposed people to` IS A `What the incident exposed people to` @desc Did the incident expose a worker or anyone else to a serious risk to health or safety from an immediate or imminent exposure to one of these? Choose the first that fits.
      `it is of a kind the Regulations exclude` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the injury, illness or incident of a kind the Work Health and Safety Regulations exclude? Answer no if you do not know of such an exclusion.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 35 to 37 -- was it a notifiable incident` `a person died` `what the injury or illness needed` `what the incident exposed people to` `it is of a kind the Regulations exclude` MEANS
    IF `a person died`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `a listed injury or illness` OR `a listed dangerous incident`
         THEN JUST (NOT `it is of a kind the Regulations exclude`)
         ELSE IF `it is of a kind the Regulations exclude`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF (`what the injury or illness needed` EQUALS `none of these`) OR (`what the incident exposed people to` EQUALS `something else`)
                   THEN NOTHING
                   ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a listed injury or illness` MEANS
            (NOT (`what the injury or illness needed` EQUALS `none of these`))
            AND (NOT (`what the injury or illness needed` EQUALS `there was no injury or illness`))
        `a listed dangerous incident` MEANS
            (NOT (`what the incident exposed people to` EQUALS `something else`))
            AND (NOT (`what the incident exposed people to` EQUALS `there was no such exposure`))

§§ `Part 5 Division 6 -- stopping unsafe work` -- arises only if the worker stopped, or wants to stop, work

-- s 84: "A worker may cease, or refuse to carry out, work if the worker has a reasonable concern that to carry out the
-- work would expose the worker to a serious risk to the worker's health or safety, emanating from an immediate or
-- imminent exposure to a hazard." s 103: "Nothing in this Part applies to a worker who is a prisoner in custody in a
-- custodial correctional facility". A permission introduced by "if": when it fails, JUST FALSE; for a prisoner in
-- custody, JUST FALSE (a flat "nothing in this Part applies").
@export May I stop or refuse work because it is unsafe (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 84)? Yes, if you have a reasonable concern that doing it would expose you to a serious risk to your health or safety from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard. You must then tell the business as soon as practicable and stay available for suitable alternative work (s 86).
GIVEN `I am a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you carry out work for a business or undertaking (as an employee, contractor, labour-hire worker, apprentice, trainee, work-experience student, volunteer or otherwise)?
      `I have a reasonable concern of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your concern reasonable that doing the work would expose you to a serious risk to your health or safety, from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard?
      `I am a prisoner in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a prisoner in custody in a custodial correctional facility?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84 -- may I stop unsafe work` `I am a worker` `I have a reasonable concern of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard` `I am a prisoner in custody` MEANS
    IF `I am a prisoner in custody`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST (`I am a worker` AND `I have a reasonable concern of a serious risk from an immediate or imminent hazard`)

-- s 88: "If a worker ceases work under this Division, that action does not affect the continuity of engagement of the
-- worker for prescribed purposes if the worker has not unreasonably failed to comply with a direction to carry out
-- suitable alternative work: (a) at the same or another workplace; and (b) that was safe and appropriate for the worker
-- to carry out." An "if": when the worker unreasonably refused safe and appropriate alternative work, the text's no
-- (JUST FALSE) to the protection; when the worker did not cease work under the Division, the section does not speak
-- (NOTHING). "Prescribed purposes" are the Regulations' (not deposited).
@export If I stopped unsafe work, is my continuity of employment or engagement protected (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 88)? Yes, for the purposes the Regulations prescribe, unless you unreasonably failed to follow a direction to do suitable alternative work that was safe and appropriate for you.
GIVEN `I ceased work under s 84 or on a representative's s 85 direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stop or refuse work under your s 84 right, or on a direction from your health and safety representative under s 85?
      `I unreasonably failed to do safe and appropriate alternative work I was directed to do` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you directed to do suitable alternative work that was safe and appropriate for you, and did you unreasonably fail to do it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88 -- is my continuity of engagement kept` `I ceased work under s 84 or on a representative's s 85 direction` `I unreasonably failed to do safe and appropriate alternative work I was directed to do` MEANS
    IF NOT `I ceased work under s 84 or on a representative's s 85 direction`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (NOT `I unreasonably failed to do safe and appropriate alternative work I was directed to do`)

§§ `Part 2 Divisions 5 and 6 -- what an offender faces` -- arises only if a duty was broken

-- ss 31, 32, 33 (maximum penalties, three tiers of offender each) and s 34B (industrial manslaughter: "(a) for an
-- individual -- imprisonment for life; or (b) for a body corporate -- 65 000 penalty units").
DECLARE `The offence` IS ONE OF
    `industrial manslaughter (s 34B)`
    `a Category 1 offence: reckless conduct (s 31)`
    `a Category 2 offence: failing a duty, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)`
    `a Category 3 offence: failing a duty (s 33)`
    `discriminatory, coercive or misleading conduct (ss 104, 107, 108, 109)`
    `another offence against the Act`

DECLARE `The offender` IS ONE OF
    `an individual, not as a business or undertaking or its officer`
    `an individual conducting a business or undertaking, or an officer of one`
    `a body corporate`

DECLARE `Maximum penalty` IS ONE OF
    `a fine of up to` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `a fine of up to, or imprisonment for up to, or both` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER, `years` IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment for life`
    `a fine of up to, in penalty units` HAS `penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `none: only a business or undertaking, or its officer, can commit industrial manslaughter (s 34B(1)(b))`
    `not answered here`

-- s 31(1): "(a) ... individual (other than as a person conducting a business or undertaking or as an officer ...) --
-- $300 000 or imprisonment for 5 years or both; (b) ... as a person conducting a business or undertaking or as an
-- officer ... -- $600 000 or imprisonment for 5 years or both; (c) ... body corporate -- $3 000 000." s 32: $150 000;
-- $300 000; $1 500 000. s 33: $50 000; $100 000; $500 000. ss 104, 107, 108, 109: "(a) in the case of an individual --
-- $100 000; or (b) in the case of a body corporate -- $500 000." Other offences: not answered here.
@export What is the most an offender can be sentenced to for this offence (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 31 to 34B, 104 to 109)? The maximum the section states, which depends on whether the offender is an individual, a business or officer, or a body corporate.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The offence` @desc Which offence?
      `the offender` IS A `The offender` @desc Who is the offender: an individual acting other than as a business or its officer (for example a worker), an individual conducting a business or undertaking or an officer of one, or a body corporate (a company)?
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
`the most an offender can get` `the offence` `the offender` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `industrial manslaughter (s 34B)` THEN
        IF `the offender` EQUALS `a body corporate`
        THEN `a fine of up to, in penalty units` 65000
        ELSE IF `the offender` EQUALS `an individual conducting a business or undertaking, or an officer of one`
             THEN `imprisonment for life`
             ELSE `none: only a business or undertaking, or its officer, can commit industrial manslaughter (s 34B(1)(b))`
    WHEN `a Category 1 offence: reckless conduct (s 31)` THEN
        IF `the offender` EQUALS `a body corporate`
        THEN `a fine of up to` 3000000
        ELSE IF `the offender` EQUALS `an individual conducting a business or undertaking, or an officer of one`
             THEN `a fine of up to, or imprisonment for up to, or both` 600000 5
             ELSE `a fine of up to, or imprisonment for up to, or both` 300000 5
    WHEN `a Category 2 offence: failing a duty, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` THEN
        `a fine of up to` (`by offender` 150000 300000 1500000)
    WHEN `a Category 3 offence: failing a duty (s 33)` THEN
        `a fine of up to` (`by offender` 50000 100000 500000)
    WHEN `discriminatory, coercive or misleading conduct (ss 104, 107, 108, 109)` THEN
        IF `the offender` EQUALS `a body corporate`
        THEN `a fine of up to` 500000
        ELSE `a fine of up to` 100000
    OTHERWISE `not answered here`
    WHERE
        `by offender` `other individual` `business or officer` `body corporate` MEANS
            IF `the offender` EQUALS `a body corporate`
            THEN `body corporate`
            ELSE IF `the offender` EQUALS `an individual conducting a business or undertaking, or an officer of one`
                 THEN `business or officer`
                 ELSE `other individual`

§§ `Part 6 -- if I was punished, pressured or misled for a safety reason` -- arises only if something was done to the person

-- s 105(1): "a person engages in discriminatory conduct if: (a) the person: (i) dismisses a worker; or (ii) terminates a
-- contract for services with a worker; or (iii) puts a worker to his or her detriment in the engagement of the worker;
-- or (iv) alters the position of a worker to the worker's detriment; or (b) the person: (i) refuses or fails to offer to
-- engage a prospective worker; or (ii) treats a prospective worker less favourably than another prospective worker would
-- be treated in offering terms of engagement; or (c) the person terminates a commercial arrangement with another person;
-- or (d) the person refuses or fails to enter into a commercial arrangement with another person." (2): organising to take
-- such action, or threatening to organise or take it, is also discriminatory conduct; folded into each choice (fork F1).
DECLARE `What they did` IS ONE OF
    `dismissed me (s 105(1)(a)(i))`
    `ended my contract for services (s 105(1)(a)(ii))`
    `put me to my detriment in my engagement (s 105(1)(a)(iii))`
    `altered my position to my detriment (s 105(1)(a)(iv))`
    `did not offer to engage me (s 105(1)(b)(i))`
    `offered me worse terms of engagement than another prospective worker (s 105(1)(b)(ii))`
    `ended a commercial arrangement with me (s 105(1)(c))`
    `refused or failed to enter into a commercial arrangement with me (s 105(1)(d))`
    `none of these`

-- A definition introduced by "if": outside its heads, JUST FALSE.
@export Is what was done to me "discriminatory conduct" (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 105)? Dismissal, ending a contract or commercial arrangement, detriment, a worse position, or not engaging or offering worse terms -- done, organised or threatened.
GIVEN `what they did` IS A `What they did` @desc What did they do, or organise, or threaten to do or organise, to you? Choose the first that fits.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 -- is it discriminatory conduct` `what they did` MEANS
    IF `what they did` EQUALS `none of these` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 106: conduct "is engaged in for a prohibited reason if it is engaged in because the worker or prospective worker or
-- the person referred to in section 105(1)(c) or (d) (as the case requires): (a) ... (j)". Paragraph (h) closes its
-- list of the people a concern is raised with (fork F2).
DECLARE `Why they did it` IS ONE OF
    `I am, was or proposed to be a health and safety representative or committee member (s 106(a))`
    `I took on, or proposed to take on, another role under the Act (s 106(b))`
    `I acted, or proposed to act, as a health and safety representative or committee member (s 106(c))`
    `I exercised, or proposed to exercise, a power under the Act, such as stopping unsafe work (s 106(d))`
    `I performed, or proposed to perform, a function under the Act (s 106(e))`
    `I refrained, or proposed to refrain, from exercising a power or performing a function under the Act (s 106(f))`
    `I assisted, or gave information to, someone exercising a power or function under the Act (s 106(g))`
    `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern (s 106(h))`
    `I was involved in resolving a health and safety issue under the Act (s 106(i))`
    `I sought compliance by someone with a duty or obligation under the Act (s 106(j))`
    `another reason`

DECLARE `Whom I raised it with` IS ONE OF
    `the business or undertaking (s 106(h)(i))`
    `an inspector (s 106(h)(ii))`
    `a WHS entry permit holder (s 106(h)(iii))`
    `a health and safety representative (s 106(h)(iv))`
    `a health and safety committee member (s 106(h)(v))`
    `another worker (s 106(h)(vi))`
    `another person with a duty under the Act about the matter (s 106(h)(vii))`
    `another person exercising a power or performing a function under the Act (s 106(h)(viii))`
    `someone else, such as the media, a family member or a friend`
    `I did not raise an issue`

@export Was it done to me for a "prohibited reason" (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 106)? Because of a safety role, power or function under the Act, help to someone enforcing it, a safety concern raised with one of the people the Act lists, resolving a safety issue, or seeking compliance.
GIVEN `why they did it` IS A `Why they did it` @desc Why was it done to you? Choose the reason it was done for.
      `whom I raised it with` IS A `Whom I raised it with` @desc If the reason is that you raised a health or safety issue or concern, with whom did you raise it (or propose to)? Otherwise choose "I did not raise an issue".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106 -- was it for a prohibited reason` `why they did it` `whom I raised it with` MEANS
    IF `why they did it` EQUALS `another reason`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `why they did it` EQUALS `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern (s 106(h))`
         THEN JUST ((NOT (`whom I raised it with` EQUALS `someone else, such as the media, a family member or a friend`))
                    AND (NOT (`whom I raised it with` EQUALS `I did not raise an issue`)))
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 108(1): "A person must not organise or take, or threaten to organise or take, any action against another person
-- with intent to coerce or induce the other person, or a third person: (a) to exercise or not to exercise a power, or to
-- propose to exercise or not to exercise a power, under this Act; or (b) to perform or not to perform a function ...
-- under this Act; or (c) ... in a particular way; or (d) to refrain from seeking, or continuing to undertake, a role
-- under this Act." (2): taking action includes not taking a particular action. (3): "a reasonable direction given by an
-- emergency services worker in an emergency is not an action with intent to coerce or induce a person." (4): an
-- emergency services worker is a police officer, a member under the Fire and Emergency Act 1996, or a prescribed class.
DECLARE `What they tried to make me do` IS ONE OF
    `use, or not use, a power under the Act (s 108(1)(a))`
    `perform, or not perform, a function under the Act (s 108(1)(b))`
    `use a power or perform a function in a particular way (s 108(1)(c))`
    `give up seeking, or stop holding, a role under the Act (s 108(1)(d))`
    `something else`

-- A flat negative ("must not") with a closed list of aims: outside them, or for an emergency direction, JUST FALSE.
@export Was I unlawfully coerced or induced about my safety rights (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 108)? Action taken, withheld or threatened against you to make you (or someone else) use or not use a power or function under the Act, or give up a role under it. A reasonable direction by police or an emergency services member in an emergency is not coercion.
GIVEN `they took or threatened action against me, or withheld or threatened to withhold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did someone organise or take action against you, or threaten to, or withhold or threaten to withhold a particular action?
      `they meant to coerce or induce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they do it intending to coerce or induce you, or another person?
      `what they tried to make me do` IS A `What they tried to make me do` @desc What were they trying to make you (or the other person) do?
      `it was a reasonable direction by an emergency services worker in an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a reasonable direction given in an emergency by a police officer, a fire and emergency services member, or another emergency services worker?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108 -- was it prohibited coercion or inducement` `they took or threatened action against me, or withheld or threatened to withhold it` `they meant to coerce or induce` `what they tried to make me do` `it was a reasonable direction by an emergency services worker in an emergency` MEANS
    JUST (    `they took or threatened action against me, or withheld or threatened to withhold it`
          AND `they meant to coerce or induce`
          AND (NOT (`what they tried to make me do` EQUALS `something else`))
          AND (NOT `it was a reasonable direction by an emergency services worker in an emergency`))

-- s 109(1): "A person must not knowingly or recklessly make a false or misleading representation to another person
-- about that other person's: (a) rights or obligations under this Act; or (b) ability to initiate, or participate in, a
-- process or proceedings under this Act; or (c) ability to make a complaint or inquiry to a person or body empowered under
-- this Act to seek compliance with this Act." (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the person to whom the
-- representation is made would not be expected to rely on it."
DECLARE `What I was misled about` IS ONE OF
    `my rights or obligations under the Act (s 109(1)(a))`
    `whether I can start or take part in a process or proceeding under the Act (s 109(1)(b))`
    `whether I can complain or inquire to someone who enforces the Act (s 109(1)(c))`
    `something else`

@export Was I unlawfully misled about my safety rights (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 109)? A false or misleading statement made to you knowingly or recklessly about your rights or obligations under the Act, your ability to start or take part in a process under it, or to complain to someone who enforces it, if you would be expected to rely on it. This is an offence only; it gives no court claim of your own (s 112).
GIVEN `it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you were told false or misleading?
      `they knew, or were reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who told you know it was false or misleading, or were they reckless about it?
      `what I was misled about` IS A `What I was misled about` @desc What was it about?
      `I would be expected to rely on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would a person in your position be expected to rely on it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109 -- was it prohibited misrepresentation` `it was false or misleading` `they knew, or were reckless` `what I was misled about` `I would be expected to rely on it` MEANS
    JUST (    `it was false or misleading`
          AND `they knew, or were reckless`
          AND (NOT (`what I was misled about` EQUALS `something else`))
          AND `I would be expected to rely on it`)

-- s 104(1): "A person must not engage in discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason." (2): "A person commits an
-- offence under subsection (1) only if the reason referred to in section 106 was the dominant reason for the
-- discriminatory conduct." (3): s 12B (strict liability) does not apply, so the Criminal Code's default fault element for
-- conduct, intention, applies (s 12A; an input). s 110(1), (2): once the prosecution proves the conduct and a s 106(a) to
-- (j) circumstance, the alleged reason "is presumed to be the dominant reason ... unless the accused proves, on the
-- balance of probabilities, that the reason was not the dominant reason". Without that, the prosecution must prove it.
@export Can the person who discriminated against me be convicted under s 104 (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 104, 110)? Only if the safety reason was the dominant reason. Once the prosecution proves the conduct and the safety circumstance, that is presumed unless the accused proves otherwise. The maximum fine is $100 000 for an individual, $500 000 for a body corporate.
GIVEN `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was discriminatory conduct engaged in against you for a prohibited reason (s 105, s 106)?
      `the accused intended the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to engage in the conduct?
      `the prosecution proved the conduct and the safety circumstance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prosecution proved the conduct was engaged in and that a s 106 circumstance (such as your raising a safety concern) existed at the time?
      `the accused proved the reason was not the dominant one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the accused proved, on the balance of probabilities, that the safety reason was not the dominant reason?
      `the prosecution proved the reason was the dominant one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the prosecution has not proved the conduct and the circumstance: has it proved the safety reason was the dominant reason?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 104, 110 -- are the elements of the offence made out` `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `the accused intended the conduct` `the prosecution proved the conduct and the safety circumstance` `the accused proved the reason was not the dominant one` `the prosecution proved the reason was the dominant one` MEANS
    IF NOT (`discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` AND `the accused intended the conduct`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the prosecution proved the conduct and the safety circumstance`
         THEN JUST (NOT `the accused proved the reason was not the dominant one`)
         ELSE JUST `the prosecution proved the reason was the dominant one`

DECLARE `Order` IS ONE OF
    `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`
    `compensation within a specified period (s 112(3)(b))`
    `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for (s 112(3)(c))`
    `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
    `compensation within a specified period, on conviction (s 111(a))`
    `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for, on conviction (s 111(b))`

-- s 111: "If a person is convicted or found guilty of an offence under section 104 or 107, the court may (in addition to
-- imposing a penalty) make either or both of the following orders: (a) ... compensation to the person who was the
-- subject of the discriminatory conduct ...; (b) in relation to a person who was or is an employee or prospective
-- employee, an order that: (i) the person be reinstated or re-employed ...; or (ii) the person be employed in the
-- position for which he or she had applied or a similar position." s 114(2): after a s 112 order about (2)(a) or (b)
-- conduct, "the court cannot make an order under section 111 ... in relation to the same conduct."
@export If the person who discriminated against me is convicted, what orders can the criminal court make for me (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 111, 114(2))? Compensation, and for an employee or prospective employee reinstatement or employment, unless the Work Health Court has already made a s 112 order about the same conduct.
GIVEN `convicted or found guilty under s 104 or 107` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been convicted or found guilty of discriminating (s 104) or of procuring discrimination (s 107) against you?
      `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, or are you, their employee or a prospective employee?
      `a s 112 order was made about the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Work Health Court already made a s 112 order about the same conduct?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order`
`s 111 -- what orders are open on conviction` `convicted or found guilty under s 104 or 107` `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` `a s 112 order was made about the same conduct` MEANS
    IF (NOT `convicted or found guilty under s 104 or 107`) OR `a s 112 order was made about the same conduct`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF `I was or am an employee or prospective employee`
         THEN LIST `compensation within a specified period, on conviction (s 111(a))`, `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for, on conviction (s 111(b))`
         ELSE LIST `compensation within a specified period, on conviction (s 111(a))`

DECLARE `What I complain of` IS ONE OF
    `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason`
    `coercion or inducement under s 108`
    `misrepresentation under s 109`
    `nothing Part 6 prohibits`

DECLARE `Their part in it` IS ONE OF
    `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))`
    `they requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted another to do it (s 112(2)(b))`

-- s 112(6): "each of the following is an eligible person: (a) a person affected by the contravention; (b) a person
-- authorised as a representative by a person referred to in paragraph (a)."
DECLARE `Who I am in the claim` IS ONE OF
    `the person affected (s 112(6)(a))`
    `a representative authorised by the person affected (s 112(6)(b))`
    `someone else`

-- s 113(1): "A proceeding brought under section 112 must be commenced not more than 1 year after the date on which the
-- applicant knew or ought to have known that the cause of action accrued."
GIVEN `the day I knew, or ought to have known` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113(1) -- the last day to start` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` MEANS
    `years after` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` 1

-- s 115: "A person cannot: (a) commence a proceeding under Division 3 of this Part if the person has commenced a
-- proceeding or made an application or complaint in relation to the same matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a
-- State and that proceeding, application or complaint has not been withdrawn; or (b) recover any compensation under
-- Division 3 ... if the person has received compensation for the matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a State; or
-- (c) commence or continue an application under Division 3 ... if the person has failed in a proceeding, application or
-- complaint in relation to the same matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a State, other than a proceeding,
-- application or complaint relating to workers' compensation." Whether "a State" reaches a Territory law (the NT
-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1992, the Return to Work Act 1986) turns on the Interpretation Act 1978 (NT), not deposited: it
-- is asked as part of the fact (fork F3, finding 4).
DECLARE `Can I start a s 112 proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may apply to the Work Health Court for an order under s 112 (s 112(1))`
    `no: nothing I complain of is conduct s 112(2) reaches (misrepresentation under s 109 is an offence only)`
    `no: I am not an eligible person (s 112(6))`
    `no: it is more than 1 year after I knew or ought to have known of the claim (s 113(1))`
    `no: I have another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter that is not withdrawn (s 115(a))`
    `no: I failed in another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter, not a workers' compensation one (s 115(c))`

-- The first failing condition is reported, in the order reach, eligibility, time, other claims (fork F5).
@export Can I take the person who discriminated against, coerced or induced me to the Work Health Court, and am I still in time (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 112, 113(1), 115)? You may if you are the person affected or their authorised representative, within 1 year after you knew or ought to have known of the claim, and you have no other live claim, and have not lost another claim, about the same matter (a lost workers' compensation claim does not count).
GIVEN `what I complain of` IS A `What I complain of` @desc What do you complain of?
      `who I am in the claim` IS A `Who I am in the claim` @desc Are you the person affected, or a representative the person affected authorised?
      `the day I knew, or ought to have known` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew, or ought to have known, that you had the claim (that the cause of action accrued). ISO date.
      `the day I would start` IS A DATE @desc The day you would start (or started) the proceeding. ISO date.
      `I have another live claim about the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you started a proceeding or made an application or complaint about the same matter under another law of the Commonwealth or a State (or, if it counts as one, a Territory) that you have not withdrawn?
      `I failed in another claim about the same matter, not workers' compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed in a proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under such a law, other than one about workers' compensation?
GIVETH A `Can I start a s 112 proceeding`
`ss 112, 113(1), 115 -- can I start` `what I complain of` `who I am in the claim` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` `the day I would start` `I have another live claim about the same matter` `I failed in another claim about the same matter, not workers' compensation` MEANS
    IF (`what I complain of` EQUALS `misrepresentation under s 109`) OR (`what I complain of` EQUALS `nothing Part 6 prohibits`)
    THEN `no: nothing I complain of is conduct s 112(2) reaches (misrepresentation under s 109 is an offence only)`
    ELSE IF `who I am in the claim` EQUALS `someone else`
         THEN `no: I am not an eligible person (s 112(6))`
         ELSE IF `the day I would start` `falls after` (`s 113(1) -- the last day to start` `the day I knew, or ought to have known`)
              THEN `no: it is more than 1 year after I knew or ought to have known of the claim (s 113(1))`
              ELSE IF `I have another live claim about the same matter`
                   THEN `no: I have another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter that is not withdrawn (s 115(a))`
                   ELSE IF `I failed in another claim about the same matter, not workers' compensation`
                        THEN `no: I failed in another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter, not a workers' compensation one (s 115(c))`
                        ELSE `yes: I may apply to the Work Health Court for an order under s 112 (s 112(1))`

@export By what day must I start my Work Health Court proceeding about discrimination or coercion (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 113(1))? Not more than 1 year after the day you knew or ought to have known you had the claim.
GIVEN `the day I knew, or ought to have known` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew, or ought to have known, that you had the claim. ISO date.
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113(1) -- by what day must I start` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` MEANS
    `s 113(1) -- the last day to start` `the day I knew, or ought to have known`

-- s 112(4): a finding of discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason "only if a reason referred to in section 106 was
-- a substantial reason for the conduct". s 113(2): for (2)(a) or (b) conduct, the alleged reason "is presumed to be a
-- substantial reason ... unless the defendant proves, on the balance of probabilities, that the reason was not a
-- substantial reason". s 113(3): "It is a defence ... in relation to conduct referred to in section 112(2)(a) or (b) if
-- the defendant proves that: (a) the conduct was reasonable in the circumstances; and (b) a substantial reason for the
-- conduct was to comply with the requirements of this Act or a corresponding WHS law." Neither applies to s 108.
-- s 112(3)(b): compensation only for (2)(a) or (b) conduct; (c): reinstatement or employment only for (2)(a) conduct
-- and an employee or prospective employee. s 114(3): after a s 111 order, no s 112 order about (2)(a) or (b) conduct
-- that is the same conduct. s 115(b): no compensation recovered under Division 3 after compensation for the matter under
-- a law of the Commonwealth or a State. Fork F6: once a bar or the defence is proved, no order is listed.
@export What orders can the Work Health Court make for me (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 112(3), (4), 113(2), (3), 114(3), 115(b))? For discrimination: an injunction, compensation, reinstatement or employment (if they did it themselves and you are or were an employee or prospective employee), and any other appropriate order. For coercion under s 108: an injunction or any other appropriate order.
GIVEN `what I complain of` IS A `What I complain of` @desc What do you complain of?
      `their part in it` IS A `Their part in it` @desc Did the person you are suing do it themselves, or request, instruct, induce, encourage, authorise or assist someone else to do it?
      `they proved the safety reason was not a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other side proved, on the balance of probabilities, that the safety reason was not a substantial reason for what was done?
      `they proved their conduct was reasonable and substantially to comply with a WHS law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other side proved both that what they did was reasonable in the circumstances and that a substantial reason for it was to comply with this Act or a corresponding WHS law?
      `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, or are you, their employee or a prospective employee?
      `a s 111 order was made about the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a criminal court already made a s 111 compensation or reinstatement order about the same conduct?
      `I have received compensation for the matter under another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received compensation for the matter under a law of the Commonwealth or a State (or, if it counts as one, a Territory)?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order`
`s 112(3) -- what orders can the court make` `what I complain of` `their part in it` `they proved the safety reason was not a substantial reason` `they proved their conduct was reasonable and substantially to comply with a WHS law` `I was or am an employee or prospective employee` `a s 111 order was made about the same conduct` `I have received compensation for the matter under another law` MEANS
    IF `what I complain of` EQUALS `coercion or inducement under s 108`
    THEN LIST `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`, `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`
    ELSE IF NOT (`what I complain of` EQUALS `discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason`)
         THEN EMPTY
         ELSE IF `they proved the safety reason was not a substantial reason` OR `they proved their conduct was reasonable and substantially to comply with a WHS law` OR `a s 111 order was made about the same conduct`
              THEN EMPTY
              ELSE concat (LIST (LIST `an injunction (s 112(3)(a))`), `compensation`, `reinstatement`, (LIST `any other order the court considers appropriate (s 112(3)(d))`))
    WHERE
        `compensation` MEANS
            IF `I have received compensation for the matter under another law`
            THEN EMPTY
            ELSE LIST `compensation within a specified period (s 112(3)(b))`
        `reinstatement` MEANS
            IF (`their part in it` EQUALS `they did it themselves (s 112(2)(a))`) AND `I was or am an employee or prospective employee`
            THEN LIST `reinstatement or re-employment, or employment in the position applied for (s 112(3)(c))`
            ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Part 13 Division 1 -- asking for a prosecution, and the time to bring one` -- arises only after an act or failure the person believes is a serious offence

-- s 231(1): "Subject to this section, a person may request the regulator to bring a prosecution if: (a) the person
-- reasonably believes that the occurrence of an act, matter or thing constitutes: (i) a Category 1, Category 2 or
-- Category 3 offence; or (ii) industrial manslaughter; and (b) no prosecution for the offence has been brought within
-- 6 months of the occurrence." (2): "No request may be made more than 12 months after the occurrence of the act, matter
-- or thing." (3): "The request must be in writing and specify: (a) the particulars of the occurrence ...; and (b) the
-- grounds for the belief that the offence occurred." (10): an occurrence includes a failure.
DECLARE `Request window` HAS
    `the first day` IS A DATE
    `the last day` IS A DATE

-- Fork F7: (1)(b) can be known to hold only once the 6 months after the occurrence have passed, so the first day is the
-- day after the day 6 months on; the last day is the day 12 months on ("not more than 12 months after").
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Request window`
`s 231 -- the window` `the day it happened` MEANS
    `Request window` WITH
        `the first day` IS `days after` (`months after` `the day it happened` 6) 1
        `the last day`  IS `months after` `the day it happened` 12

@export Between which days may I ask the regulator to prosecute (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 231)? Once 6 months have passed after the act or failure without a prosecution, and not more than 12 months after it.
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act, matter or thing (or failure) you believe was the offence. ISO date.
GIVETH A `Request window`
`s 231 -- between which days may I ask` `the day it happened` MEANS
    `s 231 -- the window` `the day it happened`

-- "may request ... if": when a condition fails, JUST FALSE; (2) "No request may be made more than 12 months after":
-- a flat negative, JUST FALSE; (3) "must be in writing and specify": a request that does not is not a request under the
-- section, JUST FALSE (fork F8).
@export May I ask the regulator (NT WorkSafe) to bring a prosecution (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 231)? Yes, if you reasonably believe a Category 1, 2 or 3 offence or industrial manslaughter occurred, no prosecution was brought within 6 months of it, you ask within 12 months of it, and your request is in writing with the particulars and your grounds.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The offence` @desc Which offence do you believe the act, matter or thing (or failure) was?
      `I reasonably believe it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your belief that the offence occurred a reasonable one?
      `a prosecution was brought within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a prosecution for the offence brought within 6 months of the occurrence?
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day of the occurrence. ISO date.
      `the day I would ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you would make (or made) the request. ISO date.
      `my request is in writing with the particulars and my grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing, and does it give the particulars of what happened and the grounds for your belief?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231 -- may I ask for a prosecution` `the offence` `I reasonably believe it` `a prosecution was brought within 6 months` `the day it happened` `the day I would ask` `my request is in writing with the particulars and my grounds` MEANS
    JUST (    `an offence a request can be about`
          AND `I reasonably believe it`
          AND (NOT `a prosecution was brought within 6 months`)
          AND (NOT (`the day I would ask` `falls before` (`the window`'s `the first day`)))
          AND (NOT (`the day I would ask` `falls after` (`the window`'s `the last day`)))
          AND `my request is in writing with the particulars and my grounds`)
    WHERE
        `the window` MEANS `s 231 -- the window` `the day it happened`
        `an offence a request can be about` MEANS
               `the offence` EQUALS `industrial manslaughter (s 34B)`
            OR `the offence` EQUALS `a Category 1 offence: reckless conduct (s 31)`
            OR `the offence` EQUALS `a Category 2 offence: failing a duty, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)`
            OR `the offence` EQUALS `a Category 3 offence: failing a duty (s 33)`

-- s 231(5): "Within 3 months after receiving the request, the regulator must give written notice of the request to the
-- following: (a) the person who made the request; (b) any person alleged to have been responsible". (6): the notice gives
-- the status of any investigation and prosecution and, if none, the reasons why not. (8): "The regulator need not give
-- the notice under subsection (5) if the request relates to an occurrence about which information is published on the
-- regulator's website." A regulative rule on the regulator, counted in days from the day it received the request.
DECLARE `Request party` IS ONE OF `the regulator`
DECLARE `Request action` IS ONE OF `give me written notice of the request (s 231(5)(a))`

GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Request party` `Request action`
`s 231(5) -- the regulator must give me notice` `days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the regulator`
    MUST `give me written notice of the request (s 231(5)(a))`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the regulator` BECAUSE "s 231(5): no written notice of the request within 3 months after the regulator received it"

GIVEN `the day the regulator received my request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 231(5) -- the last day for the notice` `the day the regulator received my request` MEANS
    `months after` `the day the regulator received my request` 3

@export By what day must the regulator give me written notice of my request for a prosecution (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 231(5))? Within 3 months after it received the request, with the status of any investigation and prosecution and, if there is none, the reasons why not -- unless information about the occurrence is published on its website.
GIVEN `the day the regulator received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day the regulator received your written request. ISO date.
GIVETH A DATE
`s 231(5) -- by what day must the regulator give me notice` `the day the regulator received my request` MEANS
    `s 231(5) -- the last day for the notice` `the day the regulator received my request`

DECLARE `The regulator's notice` IS ONE OF
    `the duty is kept, or can still be kept (s 231(5))`
    `late: no notice within 3 months after the regulator received the request (s 231(5))`
    `no notice is owed: information about the occurrence is published on the regulator's website (s 231(8))`

-- Runs the duty over what happened. A notice given on `the day asked about` stands for "had it given notice that day": if
-- that would not fulfil the duty, the regulator is late. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED
-- only. (8) "need not": the duty is lifted (fork F9).
@export Is the regulator late in giving me notice of my request for a prosecution (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 231(5), (8))? It must give written notice within 3 months after it received the request, unless information about the occurrence is published on its website.
GIVEN `the day the regulator received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day the regulator received your written request. ISO date.
      `it has given me notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the regulator given you written notice of the request?
      `the day it gave me notice` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it gave it. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `information about the occurrence is on its website` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the regulator published information about the occurrence on its website?
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about (usually today). ISO date.
GIVETH A `The regulator's notice`
`s 231(5) -- is the regulator late` `the day the regulator received my request` `it has given me notice` `the day it gave me notice` `information about the occurrence is on its website` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF `information about the occurrence is on its website`
    THEN `no notice is owed: information about the occurrence is published on the regulator's website (s 231(8))`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 231(5) -- the regulator must give me notice` `days allowed`) 0 `the events`
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the duty is kept, or can still be kept (s 231(5))`
         OTHERWISE `late: no notice within 3 months after the regulator received the request (s 231(5))`
    WHERE
        `days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the day the regulator received my request` `to` (`s 231(5) -- the last day for the notice` `the day the regulator received my request`)
        `the day of the notice` MEANS IF `it has given me notice` THEN `the day it gave me notice` ELSE `the day asked about`
        `the events` MEANS LIST (EVENT `the regulator` `give me written notice of the request (s 231(5)(a))` (`the days from` `the day the regulator received my request` `to` `the day of the notice`))

-- s 231A(1): "The regulator must seek the views of the Director of Public Prosecutions on the merits of a prosecution
-- if: (a) the regulator is considering bringing proceedings in respect of a death for: (i) a Category 1, Category 2 or
-- Category 3 offence; or (ii) industrial manslaughter; or (b) the regulator receives a request under section 231 for the
-- prosecution of an offence in respect of a death." (4): not again for a death already referred, "unless there are new
-- facts or new evidence". s 231B: "The regulator requires the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions to bring
-- proceedings for: (a) a Category 1, Category 2 or Category 3 offence in respect of a death; or (b) industrial
-- manslaughter."
DECLARE `The DPP's part` HAS
    `the regulator must seek the DPP's views on the merits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a prosecution needs the DPP's consent` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Must the Director of Public Prosecutions be involved in a prosecution about what happened (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 231A, 231B)? For a death: the regulator must seek the DPP's views when it considers prosecuting or receives a request (not again for a death already referred, unless there are new facts or evidence), and a Category 1, 2 or 3 prosecution needs the DPP's consent. Industrial manslaughter always needs the DPP's consent.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The offence` @desc Which offence is being considered or was requested?
      `it is in respect of a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in respect of a death?
      `the regulator is considering proceedings or received my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the regulator considering bringing proceedings, or has it received a s 231 request about it?
      `the death was referred before, with no new facts or evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death already referred to the DPP under s 231A, with no new facts or new evidence since?
GIVETH A `The DPP's part`
`ss 231A, 231B -- the DPP's part` `the offence` `it is in respect of a death` `the regulator is considering proceedings or received my request` `the death was referred before, with no new facts or evidence` MEANS
    `The DPP's part` WITH
        `the regulator must seek the DPP's views on the merits` IS
                `it is in respect of a death`
            AND `the regulator is considering proceedings or received my request`
            AND (`a category offence` OR `the offence` EQUALS `industrial manslaughter (s 34B)`)
            AND (NOT `the death was referred before, with no new facts or evidence`)
        `a prosecution needs the DPP's consent` IS
                (`the offence` EQUALS `industrial manslaughter (s 34B)`)
            OR  (`a category offence` AND `it is in respect of a death`)
    WHERE
        `a category offence` MEANS
               `the offence` EQUALS `a Category 1 offence: reckless conduct (s 31)`
            OR `the offence` EQUALS `a Category 2 offence: failing a duty, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)`
            OR `the offence` EQUALS `a Category 3 offence: failing a duty (s 33)`

-- s 232(1): "Proceedings for an offence against this Act may be brought within the latest of the following periods to
-- occur: (a) within 2 years after the offence first comes to the notice of the regulator; (b) within 1 year after a
-- coronial report was made or a coronial inquiry or inquest ended, if it appeared from the report or the proceedings at
-- the inquiry or inquest that an offence had been committed against this Act; (c) if a WHS undertaking has been given in
-- relation to the offence, within 6 months after: (i) the WHS undertaking is contravened; or (ii) it comes to the notice
-- of the regulator that the WHS undertaking has been contravened; or (iii) the regulator has agreed under section 221 to
-- the withdrawal of the WHS undertaking." (2): a Category 1 offence "may be brought after the end of the applicable
-- limitation period ... if fresh evidence relevant to the offence is discovered and the court is satisfied that the
-- evidence could not reasonably have been discovered within the relevant limitation period." s 34E(1): "Despite section
-- 232, the limitation periods in that section do not apply in respect of industrial manslaughter." (2): "the limitation
-- periods in section 232 do prevent a guilty verdict for an alternative offence [s 31 or 32] if the proceeding for
-- industrial manslaughter was not commenced within the applicable limitation period in that section." Unlike the
-- Commonwealth Act, (b) names no "official inquiry".
DECLARE `Time to prosecute` IS ONE OF
    `at any time; but a guilty verdict for the alternative offence under s 31 or 32 needs the proceeding brought by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `at any time on fresh evidence the court accepts (s 232(2))`
    `until` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

@export Until when can the offender be prosecuted (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 232, 34E)? The latest of 2 years after the regulator first learned of the offence, 1 year after a coronial report or inquest that showed it, and 6 months after a WHS undertaking about it was breached or withdrawn. Industrial manslaughter has no time limit; a Category 1 offence may be prosecuted later on fresh evidence the court accepts.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The offence` @desc Which offence?
      `the day it first came to the regulator's notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence first came to the regulator's notice. ISO date.
      `a coronial report or inquest showed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a coronial report, or the proceedings at a coronial inquiry or inquest, make it appear that an offence against the Act was committed?
      `the day the report was made or the inquest ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the report was made or the inquiry or inquest ended. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `a WHS undertaking was given and later breached or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a WHS undertaking given about the offence, and then breached, or withdrawn with the regulator's agreement?
      `the latest undertaking day` IS A DATE @desc If so, the latest of the day it was breached, the day the regulator learned of the breach, and the day the regulator agreed to its withdrawal. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `the court is satisfied about fresh evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a Category 1 offence: has fresh evidence been found that the court is satisfied could not reasonably have been found within the limitation period?
GIVETH A `Time to prosecute`
`s 232 -- until when can they be prosecuted` `the offence` `the day it first came to the regulator's notice` `a coronial report or inquest showed an offence` `the day the report was made or the inquest ended` `a WHS undertaking was given and later breached or withdrawn` `the latest undertaking day` `the court is satisfied about fresh evidence` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `industrial manslaughter (s 34B)`
    THEN `at any time; but a guilty verdict for the alternative offence under s 31 or 32 needs the proceeding brought by` `the latest period`
    ELSE IF (`the offence` EQUALS `a Category 1 offence: reckless conduct (s 31)`) AND `the court is satisfied about fresh evidence`
         THEN `at any time on fresh evidence the court accepts (s 232(2))`
         ELSE `until` `the latest period`
    WHERE
        `the latest period` MEANS `whichever is later of` `period (a)` (`whichever is later of` `period (b)` `period (c)`)
        `period (a)` MEANS `years after` `the day it first came to the regulator's notice` 2
        `period (b)` MEANS
            IF `a coronial report or inquest showed an offence`
            THEN `years after` `the day the report was made or the inquest ended` 1
            ELSE `period (a)`
        `period (c)` MEANS
            IF `a WHS undertaking was given and later breached or withdrawn`
            THEN `months after` `the latest undertaking day` 6
            ELSE `period (a)`

§§ `Part 9 Division 4 -- compensation for an inspector's powers` -- arises only if an inspector entered, searched or seized

-- s 184(1): "A person may claim compensation from the Territory if the person incurs loss or expense because of the
-- exercise or purported exercise of a power under Division 3 of this Part" (powers relating to entry). (2): "in a
-- proceeding: (a) brought in a court of competent jurisdiction; or (b) for an offence against this Act brought against
-- the person claiming compensation." (3): "The court may order compensation to be paid only if it is satisfied it is
-- just to make the order in the circumstances of the particular case." (4): the Regulations may prescribe matters for
-- that judgment (not deposited; the judgment is an input). "if" and "only if": JUST FALSE when they fail.
DECLARE `My compensation claim` IS ONE OF
    `I may claim, and the court may order compensation (s 184(1), (3))`
    `I may claim, but the court may not order it unless satisfied it is just (s 184(3))`
    `no claim: my loss or expense was not caused by the exercise of an entry power under Part 9 Division 3 (s 184(1))`

@export Can I get compensation from the Territory for loss or expense an inspector's entry, search, seizure or other entry power caused me (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 184)? You may claim in a court, or in a prosecution brought against you; the court may order it only if satisfied it is just.
GIVEN `I incurred loss or expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you incur loss or expense?
      `it was because of an inspector's entry power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it because of the exercise, or purported exercise, of an inspector's powers relating to entry (entering, searching, inspecting, requiring documents or answers, seizing things: Part 9 Division 3)?
      `the court is satisfied it is just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is just to order compensation in the circumstances of your case?
GIVETH A `My compensation claim`
`s 184 -- can I get compensation` `I incurred loss or expense` `it was because of an inspector's entry power` `the court is satisfied it is just` MEANS
    IF NOT (`I incurred loss or expense` AND `it was because of an inspector's entry power`)
    THEN `no claim: my loss or expense was not caused by the exercise of an entry power under Part 9 Division 3 (s 184(1))`
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied it is just`
         THEN `I may claim, and the court may order compensation (s 184(1), (3))`
         ELSE `I may claim, but the court may not order it unless satisfied it is just (s 184(3))`

§§ `Part 12 -- if an inspector's or the regulator's decision affects me` -- arises only if a notice or decision was made

-- s 223(1), table: the reviewable decisions and, for each, the eligible persons. Item 13 (a prescribed provision of the
-- Regulations) is not answered here: the Regulations are not deposited. Items 4A and 4B (WHS entry permits) are the
-- union's and the permit holder's.
DECLARE `The decision` IS ONE OF
    `an inspector's decision on failed work group negotiations (s 54(2), item 1)`
    `an inspector's decision on training a health and safety representative (s 72(6), item 2)`
    `an inspector's decision on a health and safety committee (s 76(6), item 3)`
    `an inspector's decision on review of a provisional improvement notice (s 102, item 4)`
    `the regulator's refusal of a WHS entry permit (s 134, item 4A)`
    `the regulator's revocation, suspension or other action on a WHS entry permit (s 140, item 4B)`
    `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179, item 5)`
    `a decision on returning a seized thing (s 180, item 6)`
    `an improvement notice (s 191, item 7)`
    `an extension of time to comply with an improvement notice (s 194, item 8)`
    `a prohibition notice (s 195, item 9)`
    `a non-disturbance notice (s 198, item 10)`
    `a subsequent notice (s 201, item 11)`
    `the regulator's decision to vary or cancel a notice (s 207, item 12)`
    `another decision`

DECLARE `My standing` HAS
    `I am a worker whose interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the person to whom the notice was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the person entitled to the seized thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a health and safety representative whose own interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the representative of an affected worker appointed for the purpose of s 52(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the person the entry permit is for, or holds it` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The table closes the list of eligible persons ("who is eligible to apply ... (the eligible person)"): outside it,
-- JUST FALSE; for a decision the table does not list, the Act does not answer here (item 13 aside): NOTHING. Heads for
-- the business, the person with management or control, the union and (items 9, 12) the representative who gave the
-- s 85 direction are not the claimant's and are not asked. Item 4 also lists "The health and safety representative who
-- issued the provisional improvement notice", not asked.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision`, `my standing` IS A `My standing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 223 -- I am an eligible person` `the decision` `my standing` MEANS
    IF `the decision` EQUALS `another decision`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (`the decision` EQUALS `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179, item 5)`) OR (`the decision` EQUALS `a decision on returning a seized thing (s 180, item 6)`)
         THEN JUST (`my standing`'s `I am the person entitled to the seized thing`)
         ELSE IF (`the decision` EQUALS `the regulator's refusal of a WHS entry permit (s 134, item 4A)`) OR (`the decision` EQUALS `the regulator's revocation, suspension or other action on a WHS entry permit (s 140, item 4B)`)
              THEN JUST (`my standing`'s `I am the person the entry permit is for, or holds it`)
              ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `an inspector's decision on training a health and safety representative (s 72(6), item 2)`
                   THEN JUST (`my standing`'s `I am a health and safety representative whose own interests are affected`)
                   ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `an inspector's decision on failed work group negotiations (s 54(2), item 1)`
                        THEN JUST (   `my standing`'s `I am a worker whose interests are affected`
                                   OR `my standing`'s `I am the representative of an affected worker appointed for the purpose of s 52(1)(b)`
                                   OR `my standing`'s `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker`)
                        ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `an inspector's decision on a health and safety committee (s 76(6), item 3)`
                             THEN JUST (`my standing`'s `I am a worker whose interests are affected` OR `my standing`'s `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker`)
                             ELSE JUST (   `my standing`'s `I am a worker whose interests are affected`
                                        OR `my standing`'s `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker`
                                        OR `my standing`'s `I am the person to whom the notice was issued`)

-- s 224(1): internal review is for "a reviewable decision, other than a decision made by the regulator or a delegate of
-- the regulator"; s 229(1): external review by the Work Health Court of "(a) a reviewable decision made by the
-- regulator; or (b) a decision made, or taken to have been made, on an internal review". Items 4A, 4B, 5, 6 and 12 are
-- the regulator's decisions (ss 134, 140, 179, 180, 207); the rest are an inspector's (a decision of a delegate of the
-- regulator is asked as a fact: fork F10).
DECLARE `Where to go` IS ONE OF
    `internal review by the regulator first (s 224), then the Work Health Court (s 229(1)(b))`
    `straight to the Work Health Court (s 229(1)(a))`
    `no review: I am not an eligible person (s 223)`
    `not answered here: the decision is not in the s 223 table as encoded`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 224(1) -- a decision of the regulator` `the decision` MEANS
       `the decision` EQUALS `the regulator's refusal of a WHS entry permit (s 134, item 4A)`
    OR `the decision` EQUALS `the regulator's revocation, suspension or other action on a WHS entry permit (s 140, item 4B)`
    OR `the decision` EQUALS `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179, item 5)`
    OR `the decision` EQUALS `a decision on returning a seized thing (s 180, item 6)`
    OR `the decision` EQUALS `the regulator's decision to vary or cancel a notice (s 207, item 12)`

@export Can I have this decision reviewed, and where do I go first (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 223, 224, 229)? Internal review by the regulator for an inspector's decision, then the Work Health Court; straight to the Work Health Court for the regulator's own decisions.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision you want reviewed.
      `my interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a worker whose interests are affected by the decision?
      `the notice was issued to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice (or provisional improvement notice) issued to you?
      `I am entitled to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a seized thing: are you the person entitled to it (for forfeiture, the person it was seized from, or its owner if that person may not possess it; for return, the person entitled to possess it or its owner)?
      `I am an HSR for an affected worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a health and safety representative who represents a worker whose interests are affected?
      `I am an HSR whose own interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a health and safety representative whose own interests are affected by the decision (for example, the representative whose training it concerns)?
      `I am an affected worker's s 52(1)(b) representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a decision on failed work group negotiations: are you the representative an affected worker appointed for the negotiations (s 52(1)(b))?
      `the permit is for me, or I hold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a WHS entry permit decision: are you the person the permit was sought for, or the permit holder?
      `a delegate of the regulator made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision made by the regulator's delegate (rather than an inspector acting as an inspector)? Answer no if you do not know.
GIVETH A `Where to go`
`ss 223, 224, 229 -- can I have the decision reviewed` `the decision` `my interests are affected` `the notice was issued to me` `I am entitled to the thing` `I am an HSR for an affected worker` `I am an HSR whose own interests are affected` `I am an affected worker's s 52(1)(b) representative` `the permit is for me, or I hold it` `a delegate of the regulator made it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 223 -- I am an eligible person` `the decision` `the standing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not answered here: the decision is not in the s 223 table as encoded`
    WHEN JUST `eligible` THEN
        IF NOT `eligible`
        THEN `no review: I am not an eligible person (s 223)`
        ELSE IF (`s 224(1) -- a decision of the regulator` `the decision`) OR `a delegate of the regulator made it`
             THEN `straight to the Work Health Court (s 229(1)(a))`
             ELSE `internal review by the regulator first (s 224), then the Work Health Court (s 229(1)(b))`
    WHERE
        `the standing` MEANS `My standing` WITH
            `I am a worker whose interests are affected` IS `my interests are affected`
            `I am the person to whom the notice was issued` IS `the notice was issued to me`
            `I am the person entitled to the seized thing` IS `I am entitled to the thing`
            `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker` IS `I am an HSR for an affected worker`
            `I am a health and safety representative whose own interests are affected` IS `I am an HSR whose own interests are affected`
            `I am the representative of an affected worker appointed for the purpose of s 52(1)(b)` IS `I am an affected worker's s 52(1)(b) representative`
            `I am the person the entry permit is for, or holds it` IS `the permit is for me, or I hold it`

-- s 224(1): within "(a) the prescribed time after the day on which the decision first came to the eligible person's
-- notice; or (b) such longer period as the regulator allows." (3): "the prescribed time is: (a) in the case of a
-- decision to issue an improvement notice, the period specified in the notice for compliance with the notice or 14 days,
-- whichever is the lesser; and (b) in any other case, 14 days." The compliance period is read as the days from the
-- notice's issue to the day it states for compliance (fork F11).
@export By what day must I apply to the regulator for internal review of an inspector's decision (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 224)? 14 days after it first came to your notice, or for an improvement notice the shorter of that and the notice's compliance period. The regulator may allow longer.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision you want reviewed.
      `the day it first came to my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision first came to your notice. ISO date.
      `the day the improvement notice was issued` IS A DATE @desc For an improvement notice: the day it was issued. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `the day the improvement notice requires compliance by` IS A DATE @desc For an improvement notice: the day stated in it by which the contravention must be remedied. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
GIVETH A DATE
`s 224 -- by what day must I ask for internal review` `the decision` `the day it first came to my notice` `the day the improvement notice was issued` `the day the improvement notice requires compliance by` MEANS
    `days after` `the day it first came to my notice` `the prescribed time`
    WHERE
        `the prescribed time` MEANS
            IF `the decision` EQUALS `an improvement notice (s 191, item 7)`
            THEN `the smaller of` (`the days from` `the day the improvement notice was issued` `to` `the day the improvement notice requires compliance by`) 14
            ELSE 14

-- s 226(1): the internal reviewer must decide "within 14 days after the application for internal review is received".
-- (3): "If the internal reviewer seeks further information from the applicant, the 14 day period ceases to run until the
-- applicant provides the information". (4): within the time "(being not less than 7 days)" the reviewer specifies (fork
-- F12). (5): "If the applicant does not provide the further information within the required time, the decision is taken
-- to have been confirmed by the internal reviewer at the end of that time." (6): "If the reviewable decision is not
-- varied or set aside within the 14 day period, the decision is taken to have been confirmed".
@export If the internal reviewer does not decide, on what day is the decision taken to be confirmed (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 226)? 14 days after your application was received, paused while you answer a request for information; or at the end of your time to answer, if you do not.
GIVEN `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc The day the regulator received your application for internal review. ISO date.
      `the reviewer asked me for more information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the reviewer ask you for further information?
      `the day it asked` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it asked. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `the days it gave me to answer` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days it gave you to answer (the Act requires at least 7).
      `I gave the information in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the information within that time?
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc If you did, the day you gave it. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
GIVETH A DATE
`s 226 -- when is the decision taken to be confirmed` `the day my application was received` `the reviewer asked me for more information` `the day it asked` `the days it gave me to answer` `I gave the information in time` `the day I gave it` MEANS
    IF NOT `the reviewer asked me for more information`
    THEN `days after` `the day my application was received` 14
    ELSE IF NOT `I gave the information in time`
         THEN `days after` `the day it asked` (`the larger of` `the days it gave me to answer` 7)
         ELSE `days after` `the day my application was received` (14 PLUS (`the days from` `the day it asked` `to` `the day I gave it`))

-- s 228(1): "An application for an internal review of a reviewable decision (other than a decision to issue a
-- prohibition notice or a non-disturbance notice) stays the operation of the decision." (2), (3): for those two the
-- reviewer "may stay" it, on its own initiative or on application. (4), (5): on an application, a decision "within 1
-- working day"; if none, "the reviewer is taken to have made a decision to grant a stay". The regulator's own decisions
-- have no internal review (s 224(1)) and go to the Work Health Court, where s 229B(1) says the application "does not
-- affect the operation or implementation of the decision" unless the court orders a stay (s 229B(2)).
@export Is the decision stayed (put on hold) while my review runs (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) ss 228, 229B)? On internal review, automatically, except a prohibition or non-disturbance notice, which the reviewer may stay (an application for a stay not decided within 1 working day is taken to be granted). On review by the Work Health Court, only if the court orders a stay.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision under review.
      `my review is in the Work Health Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your review an external review in the Work Health Court (rather than an internal review by the regulator)?
      `I applied for a stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a prohibition or non-disturbance notice on internal review: did you apply for a stay?
      `the reviewer decided within 1 working day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you applied, did the reviewer decide your application within 1 working day after receiving it?
      `a stay was granted or ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the reviewer grant a stay (on your application or on its own initiative), or, in the Work Health Court, did the court order one?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 228, 229B -- is the decision on hold during review` `the decision` `my review is in the Work Health Court` `I applied for a stay` `the reviewer decided within 1 working day` `a stay was granted or ordered` MEANS
    IF `the decision` EQUALS `another decision`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `my review is in the Work Health Court`
         THEN JUST `a stay was granted or ordered`
         ELSE IF `s 224(1) -- a decision of the regulator` `the decision`
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE IF NOT ((`the decision` EQUALS `a prohibition notice (s 195, item 9)`) OR (`the decision` EQUALS `a non-disturbance notice (s 198, item 10)`))
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE IF `I applied for a stay` AND (NOT `the reviewer decided within 1 working day`)
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST `a stay was granted or ordered`

-- s 229(2): "(a) if the decision was to forfeit a thing (including a document), within 28 days after the day on which
-- the decision first came to the applicant's notice; or (b) in the case of any other decision, within 14 days after the
-- day on which the decision first came to the applicant's notice; or (c) if the regulator is required by the external
-- review body to give the eligible person a statement of reasons, within 14 days after the day on which the statement
-- is provided." (c) is read as replacing (a) or (b) when it applies (fork F13). (3): "the court may at any time extend
-- the period allowed for applying for a review if satisfied there is a good reason for doing so."
@export By what day must I apply to the Work Health Court for external review (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 229(2), (3))? 28 days for a forfeiture, 14 days for any other decision, after it first came to your notice; or 14 days after reasons the court required the regulator to give you. The court may extend the time for a good reason.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision you want reviewed (for a decision on internal review, the original decision).
      `the day the decision first came to my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision (or the internal review decision) first came to your notice. ISO date.
      `the court required the regulator to give me reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Work Health Court require the regulator to give you a statement of reasons?
      `the day the reasons were given` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the statement was given to you. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
GIVETH A DATE
`s 229(2) -- by what day must I apply to the Work Health Court` `the decision` `the day the decision first came to my notice` `the court required the regulator to give me reasons` `the day the reasons were given` MEANS
    IF `the court required the regulator to give me reasons`
    THEN `days after` `the day the reasons were given` 14
    ELSE IF `the decision` EQUALS `forfeiture of a seized thing (s 179, item 5)`
         THEN `days after` `the day the decision first came to my notice` 28
         ELSE `days after` `the day the decision first came to my notice` 14

§§ `Part 13 Division 8, Part 14 -- civil claims, contracts and charges`

-- s 267: "Except as provided in Part 6 and Part 7 and Division 7 of this Part, nothing in this Act is to be construed as:
-- (a) conferring a right of action in civil proceedings in relation to a contravention of a provision of this Act; or (b)
-- conferring a defence to an action in civil proceedings or otherwise affecting a right of action in civil proceedings;
-- or (c) affecting the extent (if any) to which a right of action arises, or civil proceedings may be brought, in
-- relation to breaches of duties or obligations imposed by the Regulations." Division 7 proceedings "may be brought by:
-- (a) the regulator; or (b) an inspector" (s 260; read with s 255). So the only civil proceeding the Act gives an
-- individual is Part 6's (s 112); for the Regulations' duties the Act takes no position: NOTHING (fork F14).
DECLARE `My civil claim is about` IS ONE OF
    `a breach of a health and safety duty under the Act, such as an injury at work`
    `a breach of a duty or obligation under the Regulations`
    `discriminatory or coercive conduct under Part 6`
    `a contravention of a WHS civil penalty provision in Part 7 (entry permits)`
    `another contravention of the Act`

@export Does the Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) itself give me a right to sue (s 267)? Only for discriminatory or coercive conduct under Part 6. For a workplace injury, a claim lies in negligence or workers' compensation under other law, which the Act neither creates nor takes away; for the Regulations' duties it takes no position.
GIVEN `my claim is about` IS A `My civil claim is about` @desc What would your civil claim be about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 267 -- does the Act give me a right to sue` `my claim is about` MEANS
    IF `my claim is about` EQUALS `discriminatory or coercive conduct under Part 6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `my claim is about` EQUALS `a breach of a duty or obligation under the Regulations`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 272: "A term of any agreement or contract that purports to exclude, limit or modify the operation of this Act or any
-- duty owed under this Act or to transfer to another person any duty owed under this Act is void." For any other term the
-- section is silent: NOTHING.
@export Is a term of my contract or agreement void because it tries to contract out of the Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) (s 272)? Yes, if it purports to exclude, limit or modify the Act or a duty under it, or to transfer a duty under it to someone else.
GIVEN `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to exclude, limit or modify the operation of the Act or a duty owed under it?
      `the term transfers a duty under the Act to someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to transfer a duty owed under the Act to another person (for example, to you)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 272 -- is the term void` `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it` `the term transfers a duty under the Act to someone else` MEANS
    IF `the term excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty under it` OR `the term transfers a duty under the Act to someone else`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 273: "A person conducting a business or undertaking must not impose a levy or charge on a worker, or permit a levy
-- or charge to be imposed on a worker, for anything done, or provided, in relation to work health and safety. Maximum
-- penalty: (a) in the case of an individual -- $5 000; or (b) in the case of a body corporate -- $25 000." Strict
-- liability (s 12B). A prohibition with no period of its own: WITHIN 1 stands for the one period the question asks
-- about, so that a trace with no charge ends FULFILLED (fork F15).
DECLARE `Levy party` IS ONE OF `the business or undertaking`
DECLARE `Levy action` IS ONE OF `impose or permit a levy or charge on me for work health and safety`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Levy party` `Levy action`
`s 273 -- the business must not charge me for safety` MEANS
    PARTY `the business or undertaking`
    SHANT `impose or permit a levy or charge on me for work health and safety`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST BREACH BY `the business or undertaking` BECAUSE "s 273: a levy or charge on a worker for work health and safety; maximum $5 000 (individual), $25 000 (body corporate)"

DECLARE `The charge` IS ONE OF
    `no breach: no levy or charge on me for work health and safety (s 273)`
    `breach: the business may be fined up to $5 000 (s 273(a))`
    `breach: the business may be fined up to $25 000 (s 273(b))`

@export Did the business break the rule against charging me for work health and safety, and what is the most it can be fined (Work Health and Safety (National Uniform Legislation) Act 2011 (NT) s 273)? A business or undertaking must not impose, or permit, a levy or charge on a worker for anything done or provided for work health and safety: up to $5 000 for an individual, $25 000 for a body corporate.
GIVEN `I was charged for something done or provided for work health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the business impose, or permit someone to impose, a levy or charge on you for anything done or provided for work health and safety (for example, protective equipment or safety training)?
      `the business is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business a body corporate (a company), rather than an individual?
GIVETH A `The charge`
`s 273 -- was I unlawfully charged for safety` `I was charged for something done or provided for work health and safety` `the business is a body corporate` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 273 -- the business must not charge me for safety` 0 `the events`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN `no breach: no levy or charge on me for work health and safety (s 273)`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the business is a body corporate`
        THEN `breach: the business may be fined up to $25 000 (s 273(b))`
        ELSE `breach: the business may be fined up to $5 000 (s 273(a))`
    WHERE
        `the events` MEANS
            IF `I was charged for something done or provided for work health and safety`
            THEN LIST (EVENT `the business or undertaking` `impose or permit a levy or charge on me for work health and safety` 0), (WAITUNTIL 2)
            ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL 2)
